# Copy to .env.local and fill in to use real Postgres / S3-compatible storage (docker-compose.yml or a
# real cloud instance). Leave both unset to use the zero-install local fallback (PGlite + local
# filesystem storage) — see ADR-007. Next.js loads .env.local automatically; nothing else needed.

# --- Database (packages/db) ---
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://av_inspection:dev_only_password@localhost:5432/av_inspection_tours

# --- Object storage (packages/storage) ---
# S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
# S3_REGION=us-east-1
# S3_BUCKET=av-inspection-tours
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=av_inspection
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=dev_only_password
# S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true    # required for MinIO

# --- Cloudflare Containers production deploy (see CLOUDFLARE_DEPLOY.md) ---
# These are NOT read from this file in production -- they're set as real Worker secrets/vars via
# `wrangler secret put` / wrangler.toml's [vars], then forwarded into the container by worker/index.ts.
# Listed here only as a reference for which values to gather before deploying:
#   DATABASE_URL        -> a real external Postgres (e.g. Neon free tier) -- Cloudflare has no
#                          first-party managed Postgres; local dev's PGlite fallback is dev-only.
#   S3_ENDPOINT         -> https://<account_id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com  (R2 is S3-API-compatible;
#                          the existing packages/storage/src/s3-storage.ts needs no code changes)
#   S3_BUCKET           -> your R2 bucket name
#   S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID / S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY -> an R2 API token (dashboard: R2 -> Manage API Tokens)
#   SOFFICE_PATH        -> already set to /usr/bin/soffice inside the Dockerfile -- don't override
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY   -> only needed once the paused AI pipeline (Phase 6) is resumed
